cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its preregistered results, please cite it as below."
title: "bh-automl-augmentation: preregistered evaluation of condition-transfer augmentation for low-data Buchwald-Hartwig yield prediction"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sarukkai
    given-names: Akshath
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/akshathsarukkai/bh-automl-augmentation"
abstract: >-
  Research code and preregistered confirmatory experiments testing whether
  condition-transfer data augmentation improves low-data Buchwald-Hartwig
  reaction-yield prediction. Includes canonical seven-role reaction identity,
  group-safe splits, a repository-global one-shot outer-test evaluation
  registry, hash-addressed result manifests, and two preregistered
  confirmatory experiments whose verdicts are re-derivable from committed
  artifacts.
